  <header class="breath-theory__intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Cosmic Breath theory and method</p>
    <h2 id="breath-theory-title">Inside the CU model</h2>
    <p>
      This layer distinguishes the framework’s internal propositions, its historical
      interpretations, and the limits of what its sealed records establish.
    </p>

  </header>

  <div class="theory-grid theory-grid--paired">
    <section
      class="theory-card theory-card--expansion"
      id="cu-dark-energy"
      aria-labelledby="cu-dark-energy-title"
    >
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div>
          <p class="classification">CU theoretical proposition</p>
          <h3 id="cu-dark-energy-title">Expansion and CU Dark Energy</h3>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="definition">
        Within CU, ‘CU Dark Energy’ names the framework’s internal principle associated
        with the 26-state expansion phase. It is a CU theoretical proposition and does not
        claim that CU has empirically identified the physical cause of accelerated cosmic
        expansion.
      </p>

      <div class="distinctions">
        <article>
          <h4>Within CU</h4>
          <p>
            Expansion runs from <strong>expansion-sub-ztom</strong> through{' '}
            <strong>expansion-atom</strong>. Its 26 selectable states move outward in
            structural direction. CU declares a model-level anchor of approximately
            {' '}<strong>2.8 trillion years</strong>; that anchor is not reconstructed by
            summing the individual TOM rows.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>Historical interpretation</h4>
          <p>
            Historical CU material associates expansion with ZTOM influence and
            future-memory language. Those accounts preserve earlier CU reasoning.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>Empirical status</h4>
          <p>
            The sealed authorities do not establish that historical causal account as a
            measured physical mechanism.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="theory-card theory-card--compression"
      id="cu-anti-dark-energy"
      aria-labelledby="cu-anti-dark-energy-title"
    >
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="classification">CU theoretical proposition</p>
          <h3 id="cu-anti-dark-energy-title">Compression and CU Anti-Dark Energy</h3>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="definition">
        Within CU, ‘CU Anti-Dark Energy’ names the internal principle associated with the
        25-state compression phase. CU treats it as a defined part of its own model;
        ‘non-hypothetical within CU’ does not mean that it is an observed or scientifically
        established force.
      </p>

      <div class="distinctions">
        <article>
          <h4>Within CU</h4>
          <p>
            Compression runs from <strong>compression-btom</strong> through{' '}
            <strong>compression-ztom</strong>. Its 25 selectable states move inward in
            structural direction. CU declares a model-level anchor of approximately
            {' '}<strong>308 billion years</strong>, ending at ztom’s selectable reset-pause.
          </p>
          <p>
            Compression does not pass directly into sub-ztom. The next cycle begins only
            through <strong>Begin the Next Cosmic Breath</strong>.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>Historical interpretation</h4>
          <p>
            Historical CU material describes rapid inward collapse and uses Anti-Dark
            Energy terminology.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>Empirical status</h4>
          <p>
            Those mechanism descriptions are CU interpretations, not sealed empirical
            conclusions. CU Anti-Dark Energy is not presented here as an observed,
            measured, scientifically confirmed, standard cosmological component, or
            detected force.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section
    class="theory-card theory-card--wide"
    id="tom-duration-representation"
    aria-labelledby="tom-duration-representation-title"
  >
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div>
        <p class="classification">Methodological boundary</p>
        <h3 id="tom-duration-representation-title">How TOM Durations Are Represented</h3>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="caution">
      No validated uniform derivation currently explains all sealed TOM duration strings.
      Historical calculations are preserved for provenance and future mathematical review,
      not as canonical proofs of the approved durations or model-level anchors.
    </p>

    <div class="duration-layers">
      <article>
        <p class="step">1</p>
        <h4>Exact canonical duration strings</h4>
        <p>
          All 51 TOM records retain their exact strings. They remain unchanged unless a
          future authority revision is separately approved.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step">2</p>
        <h4>Familiar summaries</h4>
        <p>
          Readable summaries translate scale without replacing the exact strings.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step">3</p>
        <h4>Declared model-level anchors</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Expansion: approximately 2.8 trillion years</li>
          <li>Compression: approximately 308 billion years</li>
          <li>Complete breath: approximately 3.108 trillion years</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These anchors are not silently derived by summing or normalizing TOM rows.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="step">4</p>
        <h4>Historical calculations</h4>
        <p>
          Historical calculations remain provenance. Unresolved or invalid derivations do
          not control canonical duration values.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <aside class="method-note" aria-label="Historical calculation cautions">
      <h4>Why the layers stay separate</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><span>2.8 trillion ÷ 4</span> does not equal <span>280 billion</span>.</li>
        <li><span>2.8 trillion ÷ 16</span> does not equal <span>28 billion</span>.</li>
        <li>
          Historical claims that all formulas converge are not accepted as canonical proof.
        </li>
        <li>
          ATOM-as-Planck-time language is superseded by the sealed atom record.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

