          <li>Historical working documents</li>
          <li>Interpretive narratives</li>
          <li>Empirical references</li>
          <li>Superseded calculations</li>
          <li>Open questions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>How authority is applied</h4>
        <p>
          Sealed authorities control state order, transitions, exact source strings, and
          approved educational helpers. Historical documents preserve provenance and
          earlier reasoning, but adopting one historical label does not make its entire
          source document canonical.
        </p>
        <p>
          Invalid or disputed historical arithmetic is not promoted as current proof.
          Future empirical references will be presented separately from CU propositions,
